{"name":"Fiery Garnet","hex":"#b71e1e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fiery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to fire.","Burning or glowing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fiery"},{"term":"garnet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard transparent mineral that is often used as gemstones and abrasives.","A dark red color, like that of the gemstone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garnet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"},{"title":"Garnet","blocks":[{"text":"Garnets are a group of silicate minerals that have been used since the Bronze Age as gemstones and abrasives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Garnet_Andradite20.jpg/330px-Garnet_Andradite20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garnet"},{"title":"Shades of red","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color red may differ in hue, chroma, lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a red or othe